      "items": [
        {
          "field": "Acceptance Criteria",
          "fieldtype": "custom",
          "from_string": "*Swatch availability*\n\n* Given a product has only one colour, when the PDP loads, then the colour is displayed as a text label (e.g. \"Colour: Bay Blue\") and no swatches are rendered.\n* Given a product has multiple colour variations, when the PDP loads, then the index image for each colour variation is displayed as a swatch.\n* Given multiple colour swatches are displayed, when the PDP loads, then the currently viewed colour variation's swatch is visually indicated as selected.\n\n*Swatch selection*\n\n* Colour variation: Given a shopper clicks a colour swatch, when the selection is registered, then the URL updates to reflect the selected colour variation without full page reload. \n* New Style Code: Given a shopper clicks a colour swatch, when the selection is registered, then the URL updates to reflect the selected colour with a new style code and a full page reload.\n\n*Index image not populated*\n\n* Given a colour variation exists but has no index image designated, when the PDP loads, then that colour variation's swatch is not rendered and the variation is not surfaced to the shopper (pending confirmation of fallback behaviour — see dependencies).",
