        {
          "field": "description",
          "fieldtype": "jira",
          "from_string": "*As a* Shopper,\n\n*I want* to see all available colours for a product and be able to switch between them on the page,\n\n*so that* I can explore the full range of colour options before choosing which to buy.\n\n----\n\nImage for reference (final design in Figma is leading):\n\n!image-20260701-114754.png|width=241,alt=\"image-20260701-114754.png\"!\n\nThis story covers the rendering of colour swatches on the PDP and the interaction logic when a shopper selects a different colour. Swatches are driven by the index image — one product image per colour variation that is designated in SFCC BM as the representative swatch image. \n\n----\n\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\n\n\n\n----\n\n*Dependencies & Open Items:*\n\n* Index image attribute must be defined at variation group level in SFCC BM and populated with sample data before this story can be built or tested — does not currently exist in the Product Catalog Sources sheet and needs to be added to the Product Attributes story (Squad A).\n* Confirm fallback behaviour when a colour variation has no index image populated — should the variation be hidden, shown as a placeholder, or blocked from publishing?\n* Final Figma design in Zimmermann Figma space is pending — swatch design and selected state must be signed off before build begins.",
          "to_string": "*As a* Shopper,\n\n*I want* to see all available colours for a product and be able to switch between them on the page,\n\n*so that* I can explore the full range of colour options before choosing which to buy.\n\n----\n\nImage for reference (final design in Figma is leading):\n\n!image-20260701-114754.png|width=241,alt=\"image-20260701-114754.png\"!\n\nThis story covers the rendering of colour swatches on the PDP and the interaction logic when a shopper selects a different colour. Swatches are driven by the index image — one product image per colour variation that is designated in SFCC BM as the representative swatch image."
        }
      ],
